{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786915181506},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to calculate how many farmers markets the U.S. has per 100,000 residents, using two data sources:\n1. https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv (farmers markets by state)\n2. https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv (census/population data)\n\nFollowing the project instructions for the xorq analyst role, I need to:\n1. First check if there are semantic models in the catalog that already have this data\n2. If not, ingest both sources as aliases\n3. Calculate the metric (total farmers markets / total population) * 100,000\n4. Verify all values with xorq_verify\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog for semantic models and existing aliases.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking what's available in the xorq catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Mfzxz5APnJvhVFRsQNoW9X","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01CD855BQ9ncZmrcx99XXyq7","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":369,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8149,"totalTokens":8528,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.001845,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01018625,"total":0.012041250000000002},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":221},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915181528,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78Fy3av3Tefdkyagv9S","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01Mfzxz5APnJvhVFRsQNoW9X","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No semantic models in this catalog — fall back to the ordinary ingest/compose flow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915187193},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01CD855BQ9ncZmrcx99XXyq7","toolName":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No aliases.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915187194},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest both datasets. I'll need to:\n1. Create build scripts for both CSV sources\n2. Ingest them into the catalog as aliases\n3. Create a derived alias that calculates farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n4. Verify the result\n\nLet me start by creating the build scripts.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest both datasets. Let me create build scripts to load them into the catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_017JVpUejaBJJavA1QMXTbeP","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py","content":"import xorq_build as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\nexpr = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con=\"sqlite:///:memory:\",\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"xorq-analyst/1.0\"})\n)\n"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Q175xUAUnWYUt6wAVKLzYU","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/census.py","content":"import xorq_build as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\nexpr = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con=\"sqlite:///:memory:\",\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"xorq-analyst/1.0\"})\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":475,"cacheRead":8149,"cacheWrite":466,"totalTokens":9104,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0023750000000000004,"cacheRead":0.0008149,"cacheWrite":0.0005825,"total":0.0037864000000000005},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":82},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915187194,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78GNFb2wcMUe9kAcZsk","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_017JVpUejaBJJavA1QMXTbeP","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 265 bytes to .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915192501},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01Q175xUAUnWYUt6wAVKLzYU","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 304 bytes to .xorq/scripts/census.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915192501},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to build these scripts and ingest them into the catalog. I'll run the xorq build commands.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01GUP5bf8iDUEcNYvyhhiCds","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-77-trx02ook && xorq build .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/fm_bp.txt 2>&1 && cat /tmp/fm_bp.txt","timeout":60}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01ADBnBwUzzQJBngkfEp6cBE","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-77-trx02ook && xorq build .xorq/scripts/census.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/census_bp.txt 2>&1 && cat /tmp/census_bp.txt","timeout":60}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":298,"cacheRead":8615,"cacheWrite":577,"totalTokens":9504,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0014900000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0008615000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.00072125,"total":0.0030867500000000005},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":30},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915192502,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78GkkSDSKbEZC8vbqra","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01GUP5bf8iDUEcNYvyhhiCds","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Building expr from .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/xorq/cli.py\", line 797, in invoke\n    return super().invoke(ctx)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/click/core.py\", line 1873, in invoke\n    return _process_result(sub_ctx.command.invoke(sub_ctx))\n                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/click/core.py\", line 1269, in invoke\n    return ctx.invoke(self.callback, **ctx.params)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/click/core.py\", line 824, in invoke\n    return callback(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/xorq/cli.py\", line 1149, in build\n    build_command(\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~^\n        script_path,\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^\n    ...<5 lines>...\n        emit_build_path_to=emit_build_path_to,\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n    )\n    ^\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/xorq/cli.py\", line 57, in wrapper\n    return fn(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/