um all states)\n2. Get the U.S. population (the \"United States\" row)\n3. Calculate the ratio\n\nLet me get the total farmers markets first.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01EtaVR2qLGaT1z4tfRCcHhA","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.aggregate(total_markets=source.farmers_markets.sum())","limit":5}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01KWBZHJzCMRWggUgVEJsVWQ","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"census","compose":"source.filter(source.NAME == 'United States').select('POPESTIMATE2025')","limit":5}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":357,"cacheRead":20315,"cacheWrite":665,"totalTokens":21351,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0017850000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0020315000000000003,"cacheWrite":0.00083125,"total":0.004661750000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":107},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915236425,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78Kzo7TDB52SEscKgkV","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01EtaVR2qLGaT1z4tfRCcHhA","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"total_markets\"\n7944\n\n(showing up to 5 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915242183},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01KWBZHJzCMRWggUgVEJsVWQ","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"POPESTIMATE2025\"\n341784857\n\n(showing up to 5 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915242183},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! So I have:\n- Total farmers markets: 7,944\n- U.S. population: 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to calculate: (7,944 / 341,784,857) * 100,000 = 2.3237 (to four decimal places)\n\nBut I need to do this calculation through the catalog system, not by hand. I should create a derived alias that joins the total farmers markets with the U.S. population and computes the metric. This is a cross-dataset metric, so I should create a build script following the pattern in the xorq-catalog skill for \"Join two sources into a derived metric\".","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I need to create a derived metric that joins these two values. Let me create a build script for the cross-dataset metric:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_019txyJEcKzhcEj4BKkYC5zS","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nmarkets = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"markets\", storage_options=so)\n\n# Read census data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"census_data\", storage_options=so)\n\n# Aggregate total farmers markets\nmarkets_total = markets.aggregate(total_markets=markets.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US population from census\nus_pop = (census.filter(census.NAME == \"United States\")\n    .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\").mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join and calculate the metric\nexpr = (\n    markets_total.join(us_pop, markets_total.k == us_pop.k)\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=markets_total.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":715,"cacheRead"